## The Shape That Earns Its Keep

Short coffin nails are not a stepping stone to something longer. They are a finished thought.

The taper works at this length. The flat tip reads at this length. The designs that suit this shape, graphic French lines, deep single tones, negative space, fine-line art, chrome, are not consolation prizes for people who cannot grow their nails long. They are the designs that look best precisely because the proportions of a short coffin hold them correctly.

The question was never whether the shape could work short. The question was whether you had seen it proven clearly enough to commit. Book the appointment, order the press-ons, or pick up a file. <strong>Short coffin nails</strong> have always been worth it.
